course: dictionary
lesson: 5624
title: Same word, different meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them show you which one is meant. The word lilac can name a plant or a colour. «Some party candles have metal salts in the wick, so their flames burn green, red or lilac.» The flames are burning in a colour, so lilac here means pale purple.
explain: «At Mum's wedding Sky is a bridesmaid in a lilac dress.» Lilac tells you what kind of dress it is, so it is describing the dress. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? If you swap in blue and the sentence still makes sense, lilac is a colour word.
explain: Now look for other clues. A lilac bush has large bunches of small, sweet-smelling flowers in spring. Words such as bush, blossom and spring tell you that lilac means the plant. Colour words tell you it means the colour. The clues decide the meaning.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Lilac» means a bush or small tree with large bunches of small, sweet-smelling flowers in spring.
fact: «Lilac» also means a pale purple colour, as in «pale lilac».
fact: Phrases such as «lilac blossom» and «a lilac bush» show that lilac is the plant.
fact: A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Some party candles burn green, red or lilac.» What colour is lilac here? | *Pale purple | Bright orange | A kind of flower | A small tree
exercise: «At Mum's wedding Sky is a bridesmaid in a lilac dress.» What is lilac describing? | A flower | *The dress | The bridesmaid's bush | The wedding
exercise: Which phrase shows that lilac means the plant, not the colour? | lilac dress | *a lilac bush | pale lilac | lilac sky
test: «Sky wore a lilac dress at the wedding.» What is lilac in this sentence? | *A colour | A candle | A bunch of flowers | A bush
test: Which word is a clue that lilac means the plant? | Wedding | *Blossom | Dress | Candle
exam: Why does the word spring help you know that lilac means the bush? | Because a bush has no colour | Because spring is a kind of dress | Because spring is a colour | *Because lilac bushes flower in spring
